{"ts": "2026-10-19T00:43:35+00:00", "event": "forecast", "slug": "2026-10-19-mc46123-2026-world-series-require-game-6", "version": 1, "source": "metaculus", "post_id": 46123, "type": "binary", "median": 0.57, "iqr": [0.53, 0.61], "community": {"cp": null, "pro": null, "gold": null, "n_forecasters": null}, "thesis": "58% of best-of-seven World Series since 1905 reached a Game 6 (68/117, Baseball-Reference), and 54% did from 2000 to 2025. A game-by-game model using the Brewers' ~61% title odds after removing the bookmaker margin (DraftKings -170) gives ~60%. The forecast is most sensitive to how big Milwaukee's per-game edge over the AL champion really is: a bigger edge makes a sweep or a 4-1 result more likely.", "mode": "initial"}
